60,"pass":true}],"assumptions":["Natural gas is modelled as pure methane, already desulphurised.","Reformer and converter reach chemical equilibrium (ideal gas); the converter uses an approach of 10 K.","Crude methanol condensation follows Raoult's law with Antoine vapour pressures; dissolved gases are let down and burnt with the purge.","Reformer furnace efficiency 92%. Compressors driven by steam turbines.","0.5% of the methanol is lost to the column bottoms and vents.","Half of the low grade heat in the reformed gas (below 350 C) drives the distillation reboiler.","Distillation reflux ratio 1.5 with 30 theoretical stages (single column in place of the usual topping and refining pair)."],"notes":[]}